<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Thanks for pulling this together, Charlie! A few thoughts:</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">On the infrastructure migration — I'd like to propose that we delay the database stateful set migration by one week. The observability team has identified a gap in our monitoring coverage for the new Kubernetes cluster. We need at least another week to get proper metrics and alerting in place before we move the databases.</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Specifically, we're missing:</p>
<ul style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <li>Disk IOPS metrics on the new CSI driver</li>
  <li>Proper PDB and anti-affinity rules for the DB pods</li>
  <li>Load testing results for the new storage class</li>
</ul>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Better to delay one week than to have an incident during migration.</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">On the Q3 OKRs — the 90% test coverage target is ambitious. Currently we're at about 62% on critical paths. I've done some rough estimation and I think we can hit 80% by end of Q3 with the current team size. To get to 90% we'd likely need dedicated time from at least one more engineer, or we need to reduce scope elsewhere.</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">I've attached a spreadsheet with the detailed breakdown per service. Happy to discuss further in the retro.</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">For the "what slowed us down" discussion item — I think one big thing was context switching. We had 4 different incidents last quarter that required 3+ engineers to drop everything for an entire day. The new on-call rotation should help, but I wonder if we should also invest in better runbooks and automated remediation.</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">See you all at 2 PM!</p>

<p style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Alice</p>

